{
  "id": "krylov-eigen-conditioning",
  "title": {
    "ja": "Krylov固有値：クラスター部分空間と非正規感度",
    "en": "Krylov eigenvalues: cluster subspaces and nonnormal sensitivity"
  },
  "method_ids": [
    "eigensolvers"
  ],
  "summary": {
    "ja": "48次のクラスター固有値と強い非正規上三角行列で、次元4/8/16/32のLanczos・Arnoldiを測ります。残差・前進誤差・固有値条件数・不変部分空間を分けます。",
    "en": "Measure Lanczos and Arnoldi with dimensions4/8/16/32 on 48-dimensional clustered symmetric and strongly nonnormal triangular matrices. Distinguish residual, forward error, eigenvalue condition number and invariant subspace."
  },
  "assumptions": {
    "ja": "対称行列の上位2固有値の間隔は1/.1/.01です。非正規行列は実浮動小数点の上三角行列でK=10/1000とし、対角が既知固有値です。浮動小数点の相似変換後に名目スペクトルを厳密真値とは呼びません。",
    "en": "Top symmetric gaps are1/.1/.01. Nonnormal matrices are actual floating-point upper-triangular inputs with K=10/1000 and known diagonal eigenvalues. Nominal spectra after floating-point similarity construction are not labelled exact truth."
  },
  "algorithm": {
    "ja": "全再直交化Lanczosと2回MGSのArnoldiで縮約し、小さい射影行列だけを密に解きます。上位2ベクトルはQRで張る空間へ変換し、符号や回転に不変な射影行列差を測ります。",
    "en": "Use fully reorthogonalized Lanczos and two-pass MGS Arnoldi; only the small projected matrix is solved densely. Compare QR-spanned top-two subspace projectors, invariant under signs and cluster rotations."
  },
  "validation": {
    "ja": "解析的対角固有値とSciPy密固有値、左右固有ベクトルによる条件数を照合します。別に構成した2×2擬固有対ではK=1000で残差約2.5×10⁻⁸に対し固有値誤差.005を示します。これは反復法が出力した失敗例ではなく、残差だけでは保証できないことを示す感度対照です。",
    "en": "Compare analytic triangular eigenvalues, SciPy dense eigenvalues and left/right eigenvector condition numbers. A separately constructed2×2 pseudoeigenpair has residual about2.5×10⁻⁸ but eigenvalue error.005 at K=1000. It is a sensitivity control, not a failure produced by the iterative solver."
  },
  "limits": {
    "ja": "NumPyの射影コアとSciPyの密参照はLAPACK基盤を共有し得るため、全面的に独立なバックエンドとはしません。解析固有値と独立構成対照を併用します。再始動、内部固有値、大規模疎行列、普遍的な単調収束は対象外です。",
    "en": "NumPy projected solves and SciPy dense references may share LAPACK infrastructure and are not claimed fully independent backends. Analytic eigenvalues and constructed controls provide additional checks. Restarting, interior eigenvalues, large sparse systems and universal monotonic convergence are outside scope."
  },
